{"type":"message","id":"23eec0b7","parentId":"85db6c43","timestamp":"2026-02-16T15:59:55.353Z","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"type":"text","text":"[Mon 2026-02-16 21:29 GMT+5:30] Investigate and fix frequent OpenClaw gateway disconnections. The user reports having to manually restart the service repeatedly. Perform a stability audit:\n\n1. Check gateway logs for crash/exit reasons (look for error patterns, panics, OOM, port conflicts)\n2. Verify the gateway process is set to run as a service/daemon (systemd, Windows Service, or process manager)\n3. Check system resources (memory, CPU) that might cause termination\n4. Identify if any plugins (like WhatsApp) are causing instability\n5. Recommend and implement configuration changes for resilience (auto-restart, watchdog, resource limits)\n6. If needed, set up the gateway to run as a proper service with restart policies\n\nProvide a detailed report with root cause and permanent fixes."}],"timestamp":1771257595344}}
{"type":"message","id":"9287ad57","parentId":"23eec0b7","timestamp":"2026-02-16T16:00:00.018Z","message":{"role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"The user is asking me to investigate and fix frequent OpenClaw gateway disconnections. They want me to perform a stability audit with specific steps. Let me break down what I need to do:\n\n1. Check gateway logs for crash/exit reasons (errors, panics, OOM, port conflicts)\n2. Verify the gateway process is set to run as a service/daemon\n3. Check system resources (memory, CPU) that might cause termination\n4. Identify if any plugins (like WhatsApp) are causing instability\n5. Recommend and implement configuration changes for resilience (auto-restart, watchdog, resource limits)\n6. If needed, set up the gateway to run as a proper service with restart policies\n\nAnd provide a detailed report with root cause and permanent fixes.\n\nFirst, I need to understand the current setup. I'm running on Windows (Windows_NT 10.0.26200). Let me start by exploring the workspace and understanding the OpenClaw setup.\n\nI should:\n1. Check if there's a gateway service installed\n2. Look for gateway logs\n3. Check system resources\n4. Examine configuration files\n5. Check for plugins\n6. Determine the best way to set up resilience\n\nLet me start by exploring the workspace and looking for relevant files.","thinkingSignature":"reasoning"},{"type":"text","text":"I'll investigate the OpenClaw gateway stability issues systematically. Let me start by exploring the current setup and gathering information."},{"type":"toolCall","id":"call_aa0ab155c6d84f0dbdd674dc","name":"exec","arguments":{"command":"openclaw gateway status"}}],"api":"openai-completions","provider":"openrouter","model":"stepfun/step-3.5-flash:free","usage":{"input":9833,"output":626,"cacheRead":0,"cacheWrite":0,"totalTokens":10459,"cost":{"input":0,"output":0,"cacheRead":0,"cacheWrite":0,"total":0}},"stopReason":"toolUse","timestamp":1771257595353}}
