{"type":"message","id":"6483ba67","parentId":"b4a06dd1","timestamp":"2026-02-16T16:01:04.828Z","message":{"role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"It appears OpenClaw might not be installed at all, or it's installed in a very obscure location. However, the task is clear: I need to investigate and fix frequent OpenClaw gateway disconnections. This suggests that the user expects me to set up or troubleshoot an OpenClaw installation.\n\nGiven that this is a sub-agent task and I'm supposed to complete it, perhaps the expectation is that I should:\n1. Check if OpenClaw is installed\n2. If not, install it or guide the user\n3. Then perform the stability audit\n\nBut the task says \"Investigate and fix frequent OpenClaw gateway disconnections\" - it assumes OpenClaw is already installed and having issues.\n\nLet me re-read the context. The user message is the task assignment. The memory file indicates that on 2025-06-17, OpenClaw was discovered at C:\\Users\\mangs\\.openclaw\\. But we're on 2026-02-16 now. Maybe the installation got corrupted or removed.\n\nGiven that I'm a sub-agent and this is my only task, I should probably:\n1. Document that OpenClaw installation is missing or not found\n2. Recommend steps to install or recover it\n3. Provide a comprehensive stability plan\n\nBut wait, I should check the current date - we're in February 2026 according to the session info. The memory file is from June 2025, so there's a gap. Maybe the user re-installed Windows or moved the installation.\n\nLet me check if there's any OpenClaw in Program Files or other standard locations.","thinkingSignature":"reasoning"},{"type":"toolCall","id":"call_cc05e5a63cc64adfa2ef4a52","name":"exec","arguments":{"command":"dir \"C:\\Program Files\" /b 2>nul | findstr /i \"openclaw\""}}],"api":"openai-completions","provider":"openrouter","model":"stepfun/step-3.5-flash:free","usage":{"input":14206,"output":746,"cacheRead":0,"cacheWrite":0,"totalTokens":14952,"cost":{"input":0,"